    "title": "Three supervisor races in the Tri-Counties have clear winners, while a fourth is up in the air - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KCLU ,\n14 hours ago The race to fill a supervisor’s seat in northern Santa Barbara County will be decided in the general election in November. Three candidates sought the Fifth District post to replace Steve Lavaganino, who is retiring. Ricardo Valencia leads in preliminary results, with 37% of the vote. The teacher and school board member could face Maribel Aguilera in November. The Santa Maria City Council member received 33% of the vote. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
